Detect RGB30 HW revision via i2c probe, steer extlinux via pxe_label_override

The Powkiddy RGB30 ships in two HW revisions with different i2c
addresses for the tcs4525 buck regulator that powers the CPU:

  v1: tcs4525 at i2c0 0x1c   (matches upstream rk3568-evb-rgb30.dtsi)
  v2: tcs4525 at i2c0 0x40   (matches upstream rk3568-evb-rgb30-v2.dtsi)

Both DTBs are otherwise identical. If the wrong DTB is loaded, the
tcs452x driver never binds, no vdd_cpu regulator exists, cpufreq
refuses to register policies and the CPU stays stuck at boot default
408 MHz (max is 1.8 GHz).

The knulli-linux tree ships both DTBs and an extlinux.conf with two
LABEL blocks (rgb30-v1 default, rgb30-v2 override). Set the
pxe_label_override env var after successful i2c probe at 0x40 so
u-boot's extlinux/sysboot parser picks the v2 label. No effect on
other rgxx3 boards.

Signed-off-by: James Pharaoh <james@pharaoh.uk>
---
diff --git a/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c b/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
--- a/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
+++ b/board/anbernic/rgxx3_rk3566/rgxx3-rk3566.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
 #include <env.h>
 #include <fdt_support.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
+#include <i2c.h>
 #include <mipi_dsi.h>
 #include <mmc.h>
 #include <panel.h>
@@ -395,6 +396,20 @@ int rgxx3_detect_device(void)
 	env_set("board_name",
 		rg3xx_model_details[board_id].board_name);
 	env_set("fdtfile", rg3xx_model_details[board_id].fdtfile);
+
+	/*
+	 * RGB30 has two HW revisions with different i2c layouts for the
+	 * tcs4525 CPU regulator (v1 at 0x1c, v2 at 0x40). Probe v2's
+	 * address on i2c0 and set pxe_label_override so extlinux picks
+	 * the matching DTB (knulli-linux's extlinux.conf ships a
+	 * rgb30-v2 label pointing at the v2 dtb).
+	 */
+	if (board_id == RGB30) {
+		struct udevice *bus, *dev;
+		if (uclass_get_device_by_seq(UCLASS_I2C, 0, &bus) == 0 &&
+		    dm_i2c_probe(bus, 0x40, 0, &dev) == 0)
+			env_set("pxe_label_override", "rgb30-v2");
+	}
 
 	/* Skip panel detection for when it is not needed. */
 	if (!rg3xx_model_details[board_id].detect_panel)
